 "instructions": "Translate every \"en\" string into Simplified Chinese (zh-Hans), game-guide register. Follow glossary.json strictly. Keep ⟦0⟧-style placeholders, numbers, units and wiki markup exactly. Return only {\"items\":[{\"k\":\"...\",\"zh\":\"...\"}]} with the same k values.",
 "units": [
  {
   "k": "appvy",
   "en": "⟦0⟧ allow the players (and the AI) to direct the development of their nation. Each country has a ⟦1⟧, representing a number of progression paths (branches) available to that nation. These paths may be based on actual historical situations or on alternative historical possibilities. The individual options can range from political, diplomatic and warfare-related focuses to more economic and research-related focuses.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "k2esk3",
   "en": "National focuses"
  },
  {
   "k": "1710fb5",
   "en": "focus tree"
  },
  {
   "k": "m0bvqm",
   "en": "Due to the semi-random nature of the AI it ensures that no two games will play out in precisely the same way. Players wishing to have a more historical-based campaign can choose to do so by ticking the ⟦0⟧ option on the country selection screen (map) just before the start of a new game. It is important to note, however, that player nations are not bound by this and as such their in-game actions can still force the AI to pick somewhat less than historical choices.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "jau9ml",
   "en": "Historical AI Focuses"
  },
  {
   "k": "1ytpbmu",
   "en": "The seven ⟦0⟧ as well as ⟦1⟧ and ⟦2⟧ have a unique national focus tree in the base game. Additional countries - ⟦3⟧ - received a unique focus tree as part of different DLCs. All other nations use the ⟦4⟧.",
   "frags": 5
  },
  {
   "k": "1jp8lnc",
   "en": "great powers"
  },
  {
   "k": "hbescl",
   "en": "Poland"
  },
  {
   "k": "m59cub",
   "en": "Finland"
  },
  {
   "k": "15pjn5u",
   "en": "as detailed below"
  },
  {
   "k": "7xn6g8",
   "en": "generic national focus tree"
  },
  {
   "k": "xt8oj6",
   "en": "Mechanic overview"
  },
  {
   "k": "121mc3a",
   "en": "Branches in a focus tree revolve around a common theme or goal with the individual focuses within intended to help in achieving that goal. Although branches are mostly isolated from each other, they will be connected (locally) if they happen to coincide over a common point."
  },
  {
   "k": "1te67p7",
   "en": "Only a single focus can be taken at a time. A 70 day focus requires ⟦0⟧ Political power to complete at a progress rate of ⟦1⟧ Political power per day, and a 35 day focus requires ⟦2⟧ Political power to complete. When completed, the player may go up to 10 days without picking a new focus and still have those days (and their accumulated Political power) count towards the new focus.",
   "frags": 3
  },
  {
   "k": "28j0a9",
   "en": "Aside from the branches' top level focuses, most other focuses have additional requirements in need of fulfillment before they can be picked. If a requirement of an on-going focus has become invalidated, the focus will either be paused until the requirement is restored (if possible) or outright be cancelled when such a thing is not easily possible. For cases such as the latter, focuses will have bypass conditions to allow the player to proceed past them - the player will be notified of the bypass within a few days (they will display a golden bracket as if completed regularly). For example, ⟦0⟧ can be bypassed if the Motorized Infantry technology has already been researched beforehand.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "1tjv8lo",
   "en": "Motorization Effort"
  },
  {
   "k": "a4ust8",
   "en": "Once a focus has started, the player can manually stop it, unless explicitly prohibited. If stopped, a maximum of 10 days of focus progress is saved. If, due to circumstances, the focus has been invalidated, the political power already spent are lost. As such, it is recommended to check all requirements and conditions regarding a focus to assess if/how they may be affected within its completion time-frame."
  },
  {
   "k": "pwx5h2",
   "en": "Accessing a focus' expanded details can be achieved by clicking or hovering over the focus. Among the information presented there are: the flavor description, its requirements, bypass conditions (if applicable) and the expected completion effects."
  },
  {
   "k": "rf0z49",
   "en": "Visual indicators"
  },
  {
   "k": "ecnhwg",
   "en": "⟦0⟧ - Players can check at a glance a focus' completion status by the background color of its name bracket. Grey bracket means available for picking, brown bracket indicates as of yet unavailability and golden bracket denotes completed focuses. On-going focuses will feature a shining overlay effect over them.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "zhawr0",
   "en": "Bracket color"
  },
  {
   "k": "8cbz9",
   "en": "⟦0⟧ - Focuses are connected by colored lines. The color indicates whether its preceding focus is completed (green) or not (light-blue). The connection may also appear as a solid or dotted line, with the former indicating a logical ⟦1⟧ and the latter a logical ⟦2⟧. For example, to pick ⟦3⟧ would require all 3 of the focuses preceding it while picking ⟦4⟧ requires only one of the 2 preceding it.",
   "frags": 5
  },
  {
   "k": "ss3gcm",
   "en": "Connection lines"
  },
  {
   "k": "14cd03q",
   "en": "AND"
  },
  {
   "k": "1io6zio",
   "en": "Special Forces"
  },
  {
   "k": "wx0cob",
   "en": "Technology Sharing"
  },
  {
   "k": "5old9x",
   "en": "⟦0⟧ - Some focuses may have the ⟦1⟧ icon appearing in-between them. The icon denotes that only one of two may be selected. Further more, depending on the focuses outgoing connections it may also exclude from picking any of the focuses connected to them further down the line. For example, choosing between ⟦2⟧ or ⟦3⟧ will make any of the other side's subsequent connected focuses unavailable for picking up until ⟦4⟧ (linked to both sides by an ⟦5⟧ connection).",
   "frags": 6
  },
